<section class="tahajjud-guide" aria-labelledby="tahajjud-guide-heading" id="tahajjud-guide">
 <header class="tahajjud-guide-heading">
  <h2 id="tahajjud-guide-heading">Tahajjud prayer: a practical guide</h2>
  <p>Tahajjud is a voluntary night prayer. The calculator above helps you find the final third of the night; this guide explains what that period means, how to pray, what you may ask Allah for, and where Witr fits.</p>
 </header>

 <div class="tahajjud-key-facts" aria-label="Tahajjud at a glance">
  <div><span>When</span><strong>After Isha, before Fajr</strong><p>The last third is especially valued, but not the only time for night prayer.</p></div>
  <div><span>Getting started</span><strong>Two rak'ahs</strong><p>A simple way to begin; other numbers of voluntary rak'ahs are possible.</p></div>
  <div><span>How</span><strong>Two at a time</strong><p>Pray with the usual movements, recitation and taslim, then make dua.</p></div>
 </div>

 <nav class="tahajjud-guide-nav" aria-label="On this page">
  <a href="#tahajjud-how-to-pray">How to pray</a>
  <a href="#tahajjud-rakats">Rak'ahs &amp; Witr</a>
  <a href="#tahajjud-duas">Duas to read</a>
  <a href="#tahajjud-beginners">Questions &amp; tips</a>
